       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum ibuprofen dose for adults.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Daily total:** The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use under supervision. Over-the-counter use is capped at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** It would raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It wouldn't add meaningful analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit either.\n\nHere are some typical adult regimens:\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed.\n- **Inflammatory conditions or higher analgesic need:** 600\u2013800 mg PO three to four times daily. Keep the total at or below 3,200 mg/day, and use the lowest effective dose.\n\n1600 mg may have been meant as the total daily dose, for example 400 mg four times daily. Please confirm the intended dose and frequency with your supervising resident or attending, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want the order as written, it will need explicit sign-off from the supervising physician."
